From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:34:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: apply the static sample mask before early sample
 counting

Vulkan performs the sample mask test before the early depth and stencil
tests and before occlusion sample counting, so an occlusion query over a
pipeline that declares early fragment tests must report only the samples
pSampleMask keeps.  Metal has no fixed-function sample mask anywhere in its
API: the only expression of one is the fragment function's [[sample_mask]]
output, and Metal's visibility counter runs before a fragment function that
declares early fragment tests.  A four-sample probe confirms it - the same
draw counts 256 samples with the output mask 0xF and 256 again with 0xA,
while the same pipeline without early tests counts 128 - which is why
dEQP-VK.fragment_operations.early_fragment.sample_count_early_fragment_tests_depth_samples_2
and _samples_4 saw exactly twice the samples they expected.

Count those samples in the fragment function instead.  A multisampled
fragment function that writes memory is invoked once per sample that
survived the early tests, with the pixel centre still supplying every
interpolated value, so adding the invocations whose own sample_id the static
mask keeps yields exactly the count the specification prefers; a probe over a
diagonal triangle with partial edge coverage matches Metal's own visibility
result sample for sample.  The count lands in the query's visibility slot,
which Metal accumulates into rather than overwrites, and the draw leaves
Metal's counter disabled so no sample is counted twice.

The counter is compiled in only for a multisampled pipeline whose static
sample mask actually discards a sample and whose fragment shader declares
early fragment tests, only while a varying component is still free, because
Metal charges one to a fragment function that writes memory and a shader that
consumes every component must keep its pipeline and report the unmasked count
instead, and never for a post-depth-coverage shader: the memory
write makes Metal shade in sample groups, and the mask such a group receives
keeps the samples the stencil test killed, so that extension keeps its mask
and the doubled count the specification permits, exactly as it already keeps
its mask rather than the pipeline-statistics counter.

That one decision is taken where the varying count is final - after the
cross-stage varying optimizer, which still shrinks it - and drives both the
lowering and the pipeline info the draw path reads, because an info bit set
without the counter would disable Metal's counter and report nothing at all.

With the count now honouring the mask, report
earlyFragmentSampleMaskTestBeforeSampleCounting.

The new kosmickrisp_early_sample_mask_count test draws a quad over the exact
left half of a four-sample target and counts it three times through a precise
occlusion query: with the mask in the fragment shader and late tests, with the
same mask in pSampleMask and early tests, and with no mask at all.  It reads
1024/2048/2048 before this change and 1024/1024/2048 after it.
